VeridianOS: drop the unused SessionManager pointer in main()

GCC reported -Wunused-variable for 'sessionManager' in main()
(src/main.cpp). The SessionManager is created for its constructor's side
effect (connecting to QGuiApplication::saveStateRequest) and is owned by
the application object; the pointer was never used. The object is still
created, only the local variable is removed. Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp	2026-10-08 17:29:57.651663489 -0400
+++ b/src/main.cpp	2026-10-08 17:30:29.495785820 -0400
@@ -93,7 +93,8 @@
     aboutData.processCommandLine(parser.get());
     CommandLineArguments::setCommandLineParser(parser);
 
-    auto sessionManager = new SessionManager(&app);
+    // owned by app; it only has to exist to answer session save requests
+    new SessionManager(&app);
 
     QQmlApplicationEngine engine;
     engine.rootContext()->setContextObject(new KLocalizedQmlContext(&engine));
